{"app":"spr-flow","version":3,"nodes":[{"id":"note","type":"info","position":{"x":-806,"y":-543},"data":{"title":"Dual-mode SPR sensor (Sebek et al. 2023)","text":"Prism K-FIR97UV (n = 1.425 at 633 nm) | 3 L WS₂ | 282 nm GeO₂ | 47 nm Ag | water, TM, 633 nm: the structure the genetic algorithm found without extra conditions (ACS Omega 8, 20792 (2023), Fig. 2). A waveguide mode of the GeO₂ film couples to the surface plasmon of the Ag film (anticrossing, g ≈ 88 meV in the article). For n_s = 1.332 the deeper dip is the lower-angle one; at 1.337 the other one: the “resonance angle” jumps by 6.78° (article), S = 1364 deg/RIU. Here, with the library data: ~7.1°, ~1420 deg/RIU (Sensitivity node).\n\nThe map (R against θ and n_s) shows the two branches and the change of the deeper one. The response is not linear: a threshold sensor rather than a linear one, as the article notes.","color":"#8a93a6","width":440,"height":290}},{"id":"prism","type":"material","position":{"x":0,"y":-142},"data":{"materialId":"K-FIR97UV","color":"#e3eef5","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"ws2m","type":"material","position":{"x":-390,"y":71},"data":{"materialId":"WS2","color":"#6f8a5e","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"ws2","type":"layer","position":{"x":0,"y":71},"data":{"label":"WS₂","thickness":1,"layers2D":3}},{"id":"geo2m","type":"material","position":{"x":-390,"y":271},"data":{"materialId":"GeO2","color":"#ece4cf","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"geo2","type":"layer","position":{"x":0,"y":271},"data":{"label":"GeO₂ waveguide","thickness":282,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"agm","type":"material","position":{"x":-390,"y":472},"data":{"materialId":"Ag","color":"#b8bcc4","indexMode":"absolute","porosity":{"$num":"NaN"}}},{"id":"ag","type":"layer","position":{"x":0,"y":472},"data":{"label":"Ag","thickness":47,"layers2D":1}},{"id":"water","type":"material","position":{"x":0,"y":673},"data":{"materialId":"user-water-1332","color":"#6f